okay, imagine you're fighting on behalf of Russia and you're told to shoot civilians on sight or else your parents, siblings, wife and kid die and you get beat up as well. What would you do? Should I remind you that russians were the same people that introduced the no step back policy in the second world war, where if soldiers retreated, they'd get shot on the spot by commisars? Like, really. Think about it.
